{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A Psalm of David. The earth is YHWH's and its fullness</b> — because there are places on earth that receive supernal power in the manner of: <i>this is the gate of heaven</i>. Therefore he began to say: <i>The earth is YHWH's</i>, because of <i>the mountain of YHWH</i>." "<b>And the meaning of: the earth is YHWH's</b> — for by way of nature it was created to be under the waters, and by HaShem's will part of it dried, and it is the exposed half. Therefore <i>for upon</i> [it]. Rabbi Moses said: <i>upon</i> means like <i>upon</i>, as in <i>the men came upon the women</i> [Exodus 35:22], and the meaning is that [the earth] was not in a straight arrangement so that human beings would live upon it, but rather that around it would be seas and rivers. Ben Balaam said: the meaning is that it [the earth] is not distant from a river or sea."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:25.306857315Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}